From: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: do not lose a decode error on a held capture buffer

When a picture is coded as more than one job -- the two fields of a field-coded
frame, or a multi-slice picture -- every job but the last keeps the capture
buffer, and v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish() applies its state only when the
buffer is finally released:

	dst_buf->is_held = src_buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF;
	if (!dst_buf->is_held) {
		v4l2_m2m_dst_buf_remove(m2m_ctx);
		v4l2_m2m_buf_done(dst_buf, state);
	}

An error on any earlier job is therefore dropped, and the frame reaches
userspace marked good while carrying a half-decoded field.  That is the worst
shape of failure available: silently wrong output that the client is told to
trust.

Demonstrated rather than argued.  Starving one field of a field-coded MPEG-2
stream -- deleting 60% of a BOTTOM field's payload, the first of its pair, so
the engine runs out of bitstream -- makes the hardware report two failures, at
picture 21 (375 of 810 macroblocks) and at picture 62.  Before this patch
userspace saw ONE flagged capture buffer out of 31; after it, two, at exactly
the dequeues matching those pictures.  The undamaged stream still reports
exactly one, so clean frames gain no false positives and the flag does not
stick.

Remember the error on the context and apply it when the buffer is released.
Clear it there, and on the paths that release the buffer without reaching the
interrupt -- setup failure and the watchdog -- and when a stream starts, so a
fresh sequence cannot inherit a previous one's failure.

Pixel output is byte-identical for progressive MPEG-2, interlaced frame-picture
MPEG-2, field-coded MPEG-2 and VP8: this changes buffer state, never data.  The
three decode gates pass and v4l2-compliance stays 49/49.

Not H713-specific.  Any cedrus user of a multi-job picture has this, and the
capability has been granted to H.264 and HEVC all along.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: https://github.com/cstenger/allwinner-h713-mainline/blob/43b2cdd4aa1b161a281db8b10f02ce70085e2d42/patches/kernel/0124-media-cedrus-keep-decode-error-across-held-buffer.patch (0124-media-cedrus-keep-decode-error-across-held-buffer.patch, commit e550bc5)
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus.h
@@ -162,6 +162,17 @@
 	dma_addr_t			scaler_buf_addr;
 	struct cedrus_dec_ops		*current_codec;
 	unsigned int			bit_depth;
+	/*
+	 * A decode error seen while the capture buffer was HELD.
+	 *
+	 * When a picture is coded as more than one job -- the two fields of a
+	 * field-coded frame, or a multi-slice picture -- every job but the last
+	 * keeps the capture buffer, and v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish() only
+	 * applies its state when the buffer is finally released. An error on any
+	 * earlier job would therefore be dropped and the frame handed to
+	 * userspace marked good. Remember it instead and apply it at release.
+	 */
+	bool				decode_error;
 
 	struct v4l2_ctrl_handler	hdl;
 	struct v4l2_ctrl		**ctrls;
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_hw.c
@@ -344,6 +344,8 @@
 	struct cedrus_ctx *ctx;
 	enum vb2_buffer_state state;
 	enum cedrus_irq_status status;
+	struct vb2_v4l2_buffer *src_buf;
+	bool held;
 
 	ctx = v4l2_m2m_get_curr_priv(dev->m2m_dev);
 	if (!ctx) {
@@ -391,10 +393,20 @@
 	ctx->current_codec->irq_disable(ctx);
 	ctx->current_codec->irq_clear(ctx);
 
+	/*
+	 * Carry an error across the jobs that share one capture buffer. The
+	 * buffer is released by the job whose source buffer does NOT ask to
+	 * hold it, and only that job's state reaches userspace.
+	 */
+	src_buf = v4l2_m2m_next_src_buf(ctx->fh.m2m_ctx);
+	held = src_buf && (src_buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_M2M_HOLD_CAPTURE_BUF);
+
 	if (status == CEDRUS_IRQ_ERROR)
-		state = VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR;
-	else
-		state = VB2_BUF_STATE_DONE;
+		ctx->decode_error = true;
+
+	state = ctx->decode_error ? VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR : VB2_BUF_STATE_DONE;
+	if (!held)
+		ctx->decode_error = false;
 
 	v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish(ctx->dev->m2m_dev, ctx->fh.m2m_ctx,
 					 state);
@@ -416,6 +428,7 @@
 
 	v4l2_err(&dev->v4l2_dev, "frame processing timed out!\n");
 	reset_control_reset(dev->rstc);
+	ctx->decode_error = false;
 	v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish(ctx->dev->m2m_dev, ctx->fh.m2m_ctx,
 					 VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
 }
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_dec.c
@@ -127,6 +127,7 @@
 
 		ctx->current_codec->trigger(ctx);
 	} else {
+		ctx->decode_error = false;
 		v4l2_m2m_buf_done_and_job_finish(ctx->dev->m2m_dev,
 						 ctx->fh.m2m_ctx,
 						 VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR);
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_video.c
@@ -990,6 +990,9 @@
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = ctx->dev;
 	int ret = 0;
 
+	/* A new stream does not inherit the previous one's failure. */
+	ctx->decode_error = false;
+
 	if (V4L2_TYPE_IS_OUTPUT(vq->type)) {
 		ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(dev->dev);
 		if (ret < 0)
